preConditionHook:
// The session has already poked beyond one side of the day's range by only a
// SMALL amount, and has now reversed and poked beyond the other side by a
// small amount too: fade the second poke, expecting a quiet two-sided day
// rather than a trend. Long is a shallow break of the session low after a
// shallow break of the session high, confirmed by a bull bar.
//
// A two-sided cousin of the one-sided repeated-failure family; the second
// break is on the OPPOSITE side, so they never fire on the same bar.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: the session starts when the
// wall-clock close date changes -- day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)),
// the slicing CloseWithinAtrOfVwap uses -- and the running session high and
// low plus a bars-into-session counter live in locals reset on that change.
//
// "Shallow" is measured against the session's own range SO FAR, taken as of
// the PREVIOUS bar: prevHigh, prevLow and prevRange are read before the
// current bar is folded in, so the extension is compared with the range it
// actually broke and the current bar cannot enlarge its own benchmark. The
// comparison is a MULTIPLICATION, not a ratio -- EL raises a runtime
// divide-by-zero on a zero denominator and a one-bar session would supply
// one.
//
// WARM-UP: every local starts at 0 as the EasyLanguage variables do. Before
// the first date change runLow stays 0.0 (no positive low is below it), so
// dnNow and shallowDn stay false and neither side can fire -- the rule is
// silent until it has seen one complete session boundary without needing a
// guard for it. Intraday bars only.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    barsIn = 1;
    runHigh = high[0];
    runLow = low[0];
    shallowUp = false;
    shallowDn = false;
    upNow = false;
    dnNow = false;
    fadeLong = false;
    fadeShort = false;
} else {
    barsIn = barsIn + 1;
    prevHigh = runHigh;
    prevLow = runLow;
    prevRange = prevHigh - prevLow;
    upNow = barsIn >= 2 && el_gt(high[0], prevHigh)
        && el_le(high[0] - prevHigh, maxExtension * prevRange);
    dnNow = barsIn >= 2 && el_lt(low[0], prevLow)
        && el_le(prevLow - low[0], maxExtension * prevRange);
    fadeLong = dnNow && shallowUp && el_gt(close[0], open[0]);
    fadeShort = upNow && shallowDn && el_lt(close[0], open[0]);
    if (upNow) shallowUp = true;
    if (dnNow) shallowDn = true;
    if (el_gt(high[0], runHigh)) runHigh = high[0];
    if (el_lt(low[0], runLow)) runLow = low[0];
}
